# Project skills (.agents/skills)

This repo ships Agent Skills under `.agents/skills/`. Prefer these project skills over user-global skills when both apply.

When a task matches a skill's description, **read and follow that skill's `SKILL.md` before implementing** — do not wait for the user to type `/skill-name`.

Check `.agents/skills/*/SKILL.md` frontmatter `description` for relevance. Installed skills (see `skills-lock.json`):

| Skill | Auto-use when |
| --- | --- |
| `vercel-react-best-practices` | Writing, reviewing, or refactoring React/Next.js code; performance, data fetching, bundle size, Server Components |
| `frontend-design` | Building or reshaping UI; typography, layout, visual direction, distinctive aesthetics |
| `ponytail` | Any coding task (write, fix, refactor, review, choose libs); prefer minimal/YAGNI; user says lazy, simplest, yagni, or complains about over-engineering |

After clone, restore skills: `npx skills experimental_install` (reads `skills-lock.json`).

Add skills: `npx skills add <repo> --skill <name>`
